# `CLAUDE.md` is a symlink to `AGENTS.md`, created by `scripts/link-agents.mjs` on install
# rather than committed. `vp create` writes agent instruction files itself, before it installs,
# and it refuses to work around a `CLAUDE.md` that is already there: generating from a template
# that commits one dies with EEXIST (when it wants to symlink) or ENOENT (when the symlink it
# finds is one degit has already broken). Leaving the path free is what keeps `vp create`
# working; `prepare` fills it in either way.
CLAUDE.md

# AI agent state. `.claude/` is a symlink to `.agents/`, so git sees these paths
# under `.agents/`; both spellings are listed so either resolution is covered.
.agents/worktrees/
.agents/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# fallow cache
.fallow/
